RaceDay — Portfolio of Evidence, Part 1

RaceDay is a planned web-based event management platform for South African running, walking, and cycling events. Part 1 documents the relational data model, planned REST API, and SQL Server database before application code is written.

Roles

•
Organiser: creates and manages their events and categories, views enrolments for those events, and records/corrects results.

•
Participant: registers an account, browses events, enters categories, views their own enrolments, and tracks personal results.

Organiser/participant authorization and event ownership must be enforced by the API in Part 2 and reflected in the MVC interface in Part 3. Public self-registration is limited to the Participant role.

Part 1 contents

•
docs/raceday-erd.png — ERD image for submission.

•
docs/raceday-erd.mmd — editable Mermaid diagram source.

•
docs/api-endpoint-plan.md — endpoint table and design assumptions.

•
docs/raceday.sql — SQL Server database creation and sample seed script.

The ERD and SQL script share six entities: AppUsers, Events, Categories, Enrolments, Results, and WeatherSnapshots. AppUsers stores both supported roles; the other entities represent events, event categories, participant entries, results, and cached weather observations.





